305,15.8,2003,52,99,27],[19306,15.5,2003,52,103,27],[19307,15.7,2003,54,104,27]],"links":[["Harding County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/new-mexico/harding-county"],["ARC or PLC in Harding County","/arc-plc/new-mexico/harding-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the 75 years on record since 1951 show January to February came in under 90% of normal 42 times on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 16 grids. In 2025, that pair hit just 26% of normal there, then April to May ran 123% and May to June 137%. The open year 2026 has been short so far, with February to March at 2% and March to April at 17% on the middle of the grids. Grid 18406 had its driest year in 2012 at 49%.</p>"}
